NNAAMMEE
     nnpprroocc — print the number of processors

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     nnpprroocc [----aallll] [----iiggnnoorree=_c_o_u_n_t] nnpprroocc ----hheellpp nnpprroocc ----vveerrssiioonn

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The nnpprroocc utility is used to print the number of processors limited to
     the cpuset(2) of the current process, unless the ----aallll flag is specified.

     The available flags are:

     ----aallll   Count all processors currently online.

     ----iiggnnoorree=_c_o_u_n_t
             The result is decreased by _c_o_u_n_t, but never below 1.

     ----vveerrssiioonn
             Print the current program version and exit.  Do not use this op‐
             tion.

     ----hheellpp  Print usage information and exit.

CCOOMMPPAATTIIBBIILLIITTYY
     This program is intended to be compatible with nproc as found in GNU
     coreutils.

BBUUGGSS
     If HyperThreading is enabled in BIOS and disabled in the kernel, the
     ----aallll option on Linux will still report all possible CPU threads.  On
     FreeBSD only active threads will be reported.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     cpuset(1)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The nnpprroocc utility first appeared in FreeBSD 13.2.

